      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "Perfect! The wiki has exactly what you\u0027re asking about.\n\nThe Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment through **[[credential-scoping]]**:\n\nA local secrets loader reads the key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup and injects it **only into the environment of the spawned child process** (either the Ingest or Query agent), immediately before that process starts. The Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated.\n\nThis design means that even if the Hub process is compromised or misbehaves, it cannot leak the credential simply by inspecting its own environment variables \u2014 the key exists only inside the short-lived child process that actually needs it to call the Anthropic API.",
      "input_tokens": 5370,
